IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `eia-core-interpretation`
IMPORT `ei6-seat`
IMPORT `ei6-part-8-4-claimant`
IMPORT `ei6-schedule-vi`
IMPORT `ei6-part-9-transitional`
IMPORT `ei6-part-8-5-cessation`

-- Worked cases for ei6-seat: at least one for every question, each in the facts a real person in the seat would state.
-- Every expected value is read from the text by hand (the section is named beside the case). The seat's answers for
-- the days of 1996, 2020 and 2021 are those of the text current to 2026-09-30.
-- Sundays used: March 15, 2020; September 20, 2020; September 27, 2020 (the text calls it "the week beginning").

§ `Part VIII.4 - who is a claimant (s 153.5)`

-- Amara, a waitress, was laid off on March 20, 2020 because her restaurant closed for COVID-19: paragraph (a).
#ASSERT `Am I a claimant for the Employment Insurance Emergency Response Benefit` TRUE TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) `ei6 seat regular benefits` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Bruno was on regular benefits and could have had a benefit period established on March 15, 2020: paragraph (b).
#ASSERT `Am I a claimant for the Employment Insurance Emergency Response Benefit` FALSE FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) `ei6 seat regular benefits` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- The day before March 15, 2020 is too early.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a claimant for the Employment Insurance Emergency Response Benefit` FALSE FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 14) `ei6 seat regular benefits` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Maternity benefits (section 22) are not among the benefits of paragraph (3)(a).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a claimant for the Employment Insurance Emergency Response Benefit` FALSE FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) `ei6 seat maternity benefits (section 22)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Sickness benefits for a self-employed person (section 152.03) are among them.
#ASSERT `Am I a claimant for the Employment Insurance Emergency Response Benefit` FALSE FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 4 1) `ei6 seat sickness benefits for a self-employed person (section 152.03)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Chen's regular benefits ended and he cannot start work because of COVID-19: paragraph (c).
#ASSERT `Am I a claimant for the Employment Insurance Emergency Response Benefit` FALSE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) `ei6 seat regular benefits` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Dana, a fisher, was paid all her Part VIII benefits and cannot start work: paragraph (d).
#ASSERT `Am I a claimant for the Employment Insurance Emergency Response Benefit` FALSE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) `ei6 seat benefits for a fisher (Part VIII)` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- Sickness benefits (section 21) are excluded by paragraph (3)(b), and are not Part VIII: neither (c) nor (d).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a claimant for the Employment Insurance Emergency Response Benefit` FALSE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) `ei6 seat sickness benefits for an employee (section 21)` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a claimant for the Employment Insurance Emergency Response Benefit` FALSE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) `ei6 seat regular benefits` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§ `Part VIII.4 - which provisions apply (s 153.6)`

-- Section 44 of the Act (repaying a payment you were not entitled to) applies (paragraph (1)(a)).
#ASSERT `Does a given provision apply to my claim for the Employment Insurance Emergency Response Benefit` `ei6 seat the Employment Insurance Act` `Part VI` 44 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE
-- Subsection 112(3) is excepted from the Part VI provisions (paragraph (1)(d)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Does a given provision apply to my claim for the Employment Insurance Emergency Response Benefit` `ei6 seat the Employment Insurance Act` `Part VI` 112 TRUE 3 FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Does a given provision apply to my claim for the Employment Insurance Emergency Response Benefit` `ei6 seat the Employment Insurance Act` `Part VI` 112 TRUE 2 FALSE FALSE
-- Section 27 of the Regulations applies (paragraph (1)(e)); section 7 of the Act does not, unless a definition or a contrary intention.
#ASSERT `Does a given provision apply to my claim for the Employment Insurance Emergency Response Benefit` `ei6 seat the Employment Insurance Regulations` `Part I` 27 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does a given provision apply to my claim for the Employment Insurance Emergency Response Benefit` `ei6 seat the Employment Insurance Act` `Part I` 7 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Does a given provision apply to my claim for the Employment Insurance Emergency Response Benefit` `ei6 seat the Employment Insurance Act` `Part I` 2 TRUE 1 TRUE FALSE

§ `Part VIII.4 - the claim, eligibility and payment`

-- Edwin claims for the two weeks from Sunday September 20, 2020, on November 1, 2020.
#ASSERT `May I make a claim for the Emergency Response Benefit for this two-week period` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 9 20) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 11 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`May I make a claim for the Emergency Response Benefit for this two-week period` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 9 27) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 11 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`May I make a claim for the Emergency Response Benefit for this two-week period` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 9 20) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 12 3))
#ASSERT `May I make a claim for the Emergency Response Benefit for this two-week period` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 12 2)
#ASSERT NOT (`May I make a claim for the Emergency Response Benefit for this two-week period` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 4 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`May I make a claim for the Emergency Response Benefit for this two-week period` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 16) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 4 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`May I make a claim for the Emergency Response Benefit for this two-week period` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 4 1))

-- Eligibility. Arguments: claimant (b); claimant (c)/(d); resides in Canada; age; earnings 2019; earnings in 52 weeks;
-- stopped working; left voluntarily; greatest run of days stopped; income in those days; greatest run of days with no
-- income; total income over four weeks; other EI benefit; provincial pregnancy; provincial new-born; CERB; CESB; received
-- the benefit for the week; not eligible only by CERB; Commission informed (CERB); not eligible only by CESB; Commission
-- informed (CESB); a later benefit period; provincial aid; section 63 aid.
-- Chidi, 34, lives in Canada, earned $30,000 in 2019, stopped working for the whole fortnight, has no income: eligible.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for the Emergency Response Benefit for this two-week period` FALSE FALSE TRUE 34 30000 28000 TRUE FALSE 14 0 14 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- At 15 he qualifies on age; at 14 he does not.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for the Emergency Response Benefit for this two-week period` FALSE FALSE TRUE 15 30000 28000 TRUE FALSE 14 0 14 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I eligible for the Emergency Response Benefit for this two-week period` FALSE FALSE TRUE 14 30000 28000 TRUE FALSE 14 0 14 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- $5,000 in either period is enough; less than that in both is not.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for the Emergency Response Benefit for this two-week period` FALSE FALSE TRUE 34 4999 5000 TRUE FALSE 14 0 14 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I eligible for the Emergency Response Benefit for this two-week period` FALSE FALSE TRUE 34 4999 4999 TRUE FALSE 14 0 14 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Stopping work for six days is not enough; seven is.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I eligible for the Emergency Response Benefit for this two-week period` FALSE FALSE TRUE 34 30000 28000 TRUE FALSE 6 0 6 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for the Emergency Response Benefit for this two-week period` FALSE FALSE TRUE 34 30000 28000 TRUE FALSE 7 0 7 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- $800 of income in those days: not eligible by (a)(v), but deemed to meet the requirements by subsection (4) (total $800).
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for the Emergency Response Benefit for this two-week period` FALSE FALSE TRUE 34 30000 28000 TRUE FALSE 3 800 3 800 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I eligible for the Emergency Response Benefit for this two-week period` FALSE FALSE TRUE 34 30000 28000 TRUE FALSE 3 1200 3 1200 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Leaving voluntarily is not stopping work; but a claimant under paragraph 153.5(2)(b) is eligible on the no-income route.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I eligible for the Emergency Response Benefit for this two-week period` FALSE FALSE TRUE 34 30000 28000 TRUE TRUE 14 0 14 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for the Emergency Response Benefit for this two-week period` TRUE FALSE TRUE 34 30000 28000 TRUE TRUE 14 0 14 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- A claimant under paragraph (c) or (d) who did not stop working: the (c) route.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for the Emergency Response Benefit for this two-week period` FALSE TRUE TRUE 20 6000 6000 FALSE FALSE 0 0 7 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Provincial money for COVID-19 and section 63 aid do not matter (ss 153.7(2), (3)).
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for the Emergency Response Benefit for this two-week period` FALSE FALSE TRUE 34 30000 28000 TRUE FALSE 14 0 14 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- The grounds of ineligibility: another EI benefit; provincial pregnancy or new-born allowances; CERB; CESB; a later benefit period.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I eligible for the Emergency Response Benefit for this two-week period` FALSE FALSE TRUE 34 30000 28000 TRUE FALSE 14 0 14 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I eligible for the Emergency Response Benefit for this two-week period` FALSE FALSE TRUE 34 30000 28000 TRUE FALSE 14 0 14 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I eligible for the Emergency Response Benefit for this two-week period` FALSE FALSE TRUE 34 30000 28000 TRUE FALSE 14 0 14 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I eligible for the Emergency Response Benefit for this two-week period` FALSE FALSE TRUE 34 30000 28000 TRUE FALSE 14 0 14 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I eligible for the Emergency Response Benefit for this two-week period` FALSE FALSE TRUE 34 30000 28000 TRUE FALSE 14 0 14 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I eligible for the Emergency Response Benefit for this two-week period` FALSE FALSE TRUE 34 30000 28000 TRUE FALSE 14 0 14 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- CERB received but then deemed eligible by subsection (5): the Commission has not told the Minister otherwise.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for the Emergency Response Benefit for this two-week period` FALSE FALSE TRUE 34 30000 28000 TRUE FALSE 14 0 14 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I eligible for the Emergency Response Benefit for this two-week period` FALSE FALSE TRUE 34 30000 28000 TRUE FALSE 14 0 14 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- CESB received but deemed eligible by subsection (6).
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for the Emergency Response Benefit for this two-week period` FALSE FALSE TRUE 34 30000 28000 TRUE FALSE 14 0 14 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- Payable for a week. Arguments: claimant; claim made; eligible; the Sunday of the week; paid or payable before September 27, 2020.
#ASSERT `Is the Emergency Response Benefit payable to me for this week` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 9 20) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the Emergency Response Benefit payable to me for this week` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 9 27) FALSE)
#ASSERT `Is the Emergency Response Benefit payable to me for this week` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 9 27) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the Emergency Response Benefit payable to me for this week` TRUE TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 9 20) FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the Emergency Response Benefit payable to me for this week` TRUE FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 9 20) FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the Emergency Response Benefit payable to me for this week` FALSE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 9 20) FALSE)

-- The amount: $500 a week; the family supplement of section 16 is added.
#ASSERT `How much Emergency Response Benefit do I get for a week` TRUE 0 EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `How much Emergency Response Benefit do I get for a week` FALSE 100 EQUALS 600
-- The maximum number of weeks: 28 less the weeks of CERB or CESB.
#ASSERT `For how many weeks at most can I be paid the Emergency Response Benefit` 0 EQUALS JUST 28
#ASSERT `For how many weeks at most can I be paid the Emergency Response Benefit` 12 EQUALS JUST 16
#ASSERT `For how many weeks at most can I be paid the Emergency Response Benefit` 29 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can the Emergency Response Benefit still be paid to me for another week` 15 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Emergency Response Benefit still be paid to me for another week` 28 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Emergency Response Benefit still be paid to me for another week` 0 29 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Duties and rights around the claim.
#ASSERT `Must I give the Minister the information the Minister asks for about my claim` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must I give the Minister the information the Minister asks for about my claim` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Must the Commission decide my claim for the Emergency Response Benefit and tell me its decision` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Commission decide my claim for the Emergency Response Benefit and tell me its decision` FALSE)

-- No benefit period. Arguments: first day; the benefit is of 153.5(3)(a); paid before September 27; weeks claimed; CERB/CESB weeks.
#ASSERT `Is a benefit period barred from being established for me beginning on this day` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) TRUE FALSE 0 0
#ASSERT `Is a benefit period barred from being established for me beginning on this day` (YearMonthDay 2020 9 26) TRUE FALSE 0 0
#ASSERT `Is a benefit period barred from being established for me beginning on this day` (YearMonthDay 2020 9 27) TRUE TRUE 10 0
#ASSERT NOT (`Is a benefit period barred from being established for me beginning on this day` (YearMonthDay 2020 9 27) TRUE TRUE 28 0)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is a benefit period barred from being established for me beginning on this day` (YearMonthDay 2020 9 27) TRUE TRUE 20 8)
#ASSERT `Is a benefit period barred from being established for me beginning on this day` (YearMonthDay 2020 9 27) TRUE TRUE 19 8
#ASSERT NOT (`Is a benefit period barred from being established for me beginning on this day` (YearMonthDay 2020 10 4) TRUE TRUE 10 0)
-- With more than 28 weeks of CERB or CESB the text gives no maximum (fork F-ei6-6); the seat takes it as 0, so no bar (assumed, not ruled).
#ASSERT NOT (`Is a benefit period barred from being established for me beginning on this day` (YearMonthDay 2020 9 27) TRUE TRUE 10 29)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is a benefit period barred from being established for me beginning on this day` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 14) TRUE FALSE 0 0)

-- The end of an earlier benefit period (s 153.121) and the weeks left out (s 153.13).
#ASSERT `On what day does my earlier benefit period end because I was paid the Emergency Response Benefit` (YearMonthDay 2020 1 5) (YearMonthDay 2020 4 5) FALSE EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 4 4)
#ASSERT `On what day does my earlier benefit period end because I was paid the Emergency Response Benefit` (YearMonthDay 2020 1 5) (YearMonthDay 2020 4 5) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On what day does my earlier benefit period end because I was paid the Emergency Response Benefit` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2020 4 5) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does my benefit period stay open, and am I treated as not eligible for the Emergency Response Benefit, after a reconsideration` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my benefit period stay open, and am I treated as not eligible for the Emergency Response Benefit, after a reconsideration` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Is this week left out when my benefit period is established` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 22) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this week left out when my benefit period is established` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 22) FALSE)

§ `Part VIII.4 - the Social Insurance Number, repayment, decisions, reconsideration, write-off`

#ASSERT `May the Minister collect and use my Social Insurance Number for the Emergency Response Benefit` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May the Minister collect and use my Social Insurance Number for the Emergency Response Benefit` TRUE FALSE)
